    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2458ah5RXUaVwK3exFed2W8)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no dependencies.\n- Safe to merge anytime: no open PR touches `sp-posframe.el` or `sp-posframe.org` (#415 to #421 and #430 are DEVONthink work; #429, the citar column revert, is already merged).\n- #429 and the citar column follow-up do not touch this module. If half-frame sizing comes back, note `sp-posframe-width-fraction` only applies while the posframe is on.\n\n## What\n\n- `sp-posframe-enabled` (defcustom, default `t`): `nil` shows the minibuffer in the normal place at the bottom of the frame.\n- Applies live: the `:set` function turns `vertico-posframe-mode` on or off, so `setopt` and Customize need no restart.\n- `M-x sp-posframe-toggle` flips it for the session; set the variable in the config to keep it.\n- Start-up reads the variable, so `nil` starts without the posframe.\n- Doc: `docs/tangles/ui/sp-posframe.org` (bullet list, tangled to `sp-posframe.el`).\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Not run in Emacs (no Emacs in the container, no GUI).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Pull this branch, restart Emacs.\n- [x] `M-x` shows the centred posframe (default unchanged).\n- [x] `M-x sp-posframe-toggle` prints \"Minibuffer posframe off\"; the next `M-x` shows at the bottom of the frame (untested by Claude).\n- [x] Toggle again: posframe is back, no restart needed (untested by Claude).\n- [x] Edge: `C-x C-f` and a note picker also follow the switch while off.\n- [ ] Edge: `(setopt sp-posframe-enabled nil)` in the init file starts Emacs with no posframe.\n- [x] Regression: with it on, width is still 75% of the frame and the padding is unchanged.\n- [x] Regression: toggling off and on does not glitch `M-x` text or overlap windows (see the history in the doc).\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 431-posframe-switch`.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Nothing touches the vault.\n- Fish works for all of it; Stow, no yadm.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB2p2pmwP3KwjhVMbg)_",
